{"name":"Gun Barrel","hex":"#979d9a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gun barrel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The barrel of a gun.","Clipping of gun barrel tank."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gun_barrel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gun Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"Gun Barrel is a German heavy metal band formed in 1998 in Cologne, North Rhine-Westphalia. Gun Barrel was founded by Guido Feldhausen and Rolf Tanzius and released their first EP Back To Suicide (2000) with the line-up consisting of Guido Feldhausen (vocals), Rolf Tanzius (guitar), Holger Schulz (bass) and Florens Neuheuser (drums). They play traditional/old school heavy metal and they personally call their musical style \"Power dive rock 'n' metal\". So far they have released six studio albums, Power-Dive (2001), Battle-Tested (2003), Bombard Your Soul (2005), Outlaw Invasion (2008), Brace For Impact (2012) and Damage Dancer (2014). Rolf Tanzius is currently the only original band member."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun_Barrel","wikidata":"Q5618294"},{"title":"Gun barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A gun barrel is a crucial part of gun-type weapons such as small firearms, artillery pieces, and air guns. It is the straight shooting tube, usually made of rigid high-strength metal, through which a contained rapid expansion of high-pressure gas(es) is used to propel a projectile out of the front end (muzzle) at a high velocity. The hollow interior of the barrel is called the bore, and the diameter of the bore is called its calibre, usually measured in inches or millimetres."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun_barrel","wikidata":"Q487192"},{"title":"Gun","blocks":[{"text":"A gun is a device that propels a projectile using pressure or explosive force. The projectiles are typically solid, but can also be pressurized liquid, or gas. Solid projectiles may be free-flying or tethered. A large-caliber gun is also called a cannon, while a hand-held gun may be called a firearm. Guns were designed as weapons for military use, and then found use in hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg/330px-SIG_Pro_by_Augustas_Didzgalvis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun","wikidata":"Q110155210"},{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel","wikidata":"Q10289"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Moscow_July_2011-10a.jpg/500px-Moscow_July_2011-10a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Moscow_July_2011-10a.jpg/1280px-Moscow_July_2011-10a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Moscow_July_2011-10a.jpg/500px-Moscow_July_2011-10a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Tsar Cannon of 1586 with its huge bore and a barrel exterior which is perceived like a stack of storage barrels","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoscow_July_2011-10a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/The_Employment_of_Women_in_Britain%2C_1914-1918_Q110352.jpg/500px-The_Employment_of_Women_in_Britain%2C_19